Docker Network:-
------------------------
A Docker network allows Docker containers to communicate with each other.

Example 1: Create a network
    docker network create employee-network

Now run PostgreSQL:
docker run -d \
  --name postgres-db \
  --network employee-network \
  postgres

Run your API:
docker run -d \
  --name employee-api \
  --network employee-network \
  employee-api-image

Now:
employee-network
│
├── employee-api
└── postgres-db

The API can communicate with PostgreSQL using its container name:

postgres-db:5432


Port Mapping:-
------------------
Port mapping allows something outside a Docker container to access a service running inside the container.

The format is:
-p HOST_PORT:CONTAINER_PORT


| Docker Network                      | Port Mapping                               |
| ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |
| Connects containers                 | Connects host/outside world to a container |
| Container → Container communication | Host → Container communication             |
| Example: API → PostgreSQL           | Example: Browser → API                     |
| Uses internal Docker networking     | Uses published host ports                  |


